    "result": "I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py` and wrote a test suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. All 33 tests pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\n`encode` groups consecutive equal characters. Runs of 4 or more become `~n~c`, and a shorter run of `~` is doubled. `decode` reads left to right, expands `~~` to one `~`, and parses runs in a helper. The helper raises `ValueError` for each malformed case in the spec: a trailing `~`, a non-digit after `~`, leading zeros, a count below 4, a missing second `~`, or a missing character after it.\n\nThe tests cover encoding examples with round-trips, the lenient decode cases, the error cases and round-trip checks.\n\nThe tests passed, but I didn't run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit checks myself, so I can't say whether they'll pass. I split the parsing into small helper functions to keep each function's complexity low.",
